WEBVTT

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.433
and --

00:06:30.457 --> 00:06:31.473
bam!

00:06:31.497 --> 00:06:33.012
We have our first stars.

00:06:33.678 --> 00:06:37.536
From about 200 million years
after the Big Bang,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.967
stars begin to appear
all through the universe,

00:06:40.991 --> 00:06:42.062
billions of them.

00:06:42.499 --> 00:06:45.355
And the universe is now
significantly more interesting

00:06:45.379 --> 00:06:46.474
and more complex.

00:06:47.928 --> 00:06:51.044
Stars will create
the Goldilocks conditions

00:06:51.068 --> 00:06:52.967
for crossing two new thresholds.

00:06:53.371 --> 00:06:55.950
When very large stars die,

00:06:55.974 --> 00:06:58.295
they create temperatures so high

00:06:58.319 --> 00:07:01.952
that protons begin to fuse
in all sorts of exotic combinations,